# Environment Variables
.env
.env.build
.vercel

# Vim swap files. Do NOT write `*.sw*`: that also swallows *.swift, i.e. the
# whole iOS app. There are two shapes to catch.
#   .notes.txt.swp        a swap for a named buffer, anywhere in the tree
#   .swp .swo ... .swa .svz .svy
#                         vim opened with NO filename, in the repo root. It
#                         walks the alphabet BACKWARDS on each new session, so
#                         any pattern with a floor (the old `.sw[c-m]`) leaks
#                         the moment vim steps past it. Four of them reached
#                         main that way. The range below covers the whole walk
#                         and is exactly four characters, so it cannot reach
#                         `.swift`; the leading slash keeps it at the root.
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
.*.sw?
/.s[t-w][a-z]
.vscode
.cursor


# tools/structgen's outputs. BUILD OUTPUTS, written by tools/structgen/gen.sh
# (and by the wasm and ios-lib make targets) on every build that consumes them -
# the web, the type-check, every test lane, the edge-function deploy, FoolishKit.
#
# They used to be committed. verify.wasm is why they are not: it sat committed
# under tools/structgen/gen/ with `diff -x verify.wasm` excusing it from the
# freshness check, and the exclusion is what let it rot for months while the
# check reported everything fresh (f6338351). An artifact nothing compares is an
# artifact nothing keeps fresh, and the cheapest way to have nothing to compare
# is to have nothing committed.
#
# e2e/validation/generated_outputs_validation.test.ts refuses a tracked file
# under any of these, and reads the directory list out of gen.sh rather than
# restating it here - so a new output is covered the day it lands.
sdk/ts/gen/
sdk/swift/gen/
sdk/kotlin/gen/
tools/structgen/gen/

# c
c/build/
# The shared toolchain's own build outputs - the generator and datagen binaries,
# and the wasm/twin links gen.sh makes. Same reason as tools/structgen/gen/
# above: built on demand by whichever libclang is on the machine, committed
# nowhere.
shared/tools/structgen/build/
shared/tools/datagen/build/
# And tighten's, which is one C file and a `make` away on any machine.
shared/tools/tighten/build/
c/*.trace/
c/tools/tt_divergence_viz/backup/
c/tools/tt_divergence_viz/backup2/
c/tools/tt_divergence_viz/data/W/

# Local scratch that has snuck into commits before: a stray vim runtime file,
# a dev server log, the iOS snapshot-test output dir, and the memtest edge
# scratch function. (Bare-name editor spill is handled in the vim block above.)
.watchrealsizevim
serve.log
ios/FoolishTests/__Snapshots__/
server/impls/supabase/functions/memtest/
# The supabase CLI's own version-check cache. Written by any `supabase` command,
# so it appears as untracked the first time you touch the CLI in a session and
# is exactly the shape of thing that rides along in a `git add -A`.
supabase/.temp/

# local dev overrides (shadows next.config.mjs if tracked!)
next.config.js

# Local Claude Code agent worktrees / local state — ignored, EXCEPT the shared
# project hook below (installs binaryen so `make wasm-bots` can run wasm-opt).
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/hooks/
.claude/hooks/*
!.claude/hooks/session-start.sh
isolate-*.log

# Coverage artifacts
.v8cov/

# Python bytecode from the QA tooling - never a repo artifact.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
